---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  A badge shows a count, or with <code>dot</code> (or no <code>value</code>) a small dot. A number above
  <code>max</code> (default 99) shows as <code>99+</code>. <code>intent</code> (<code>info</code>,
  <code>success</code>, <code>warning</code>, <code>danger</code>) sets the color.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={"html"} inline>

  <div class='badge-wrapper'>
    <wc-icon name="notifications"/>
    <wc-badge class='badge-anchor-simple' dot/>
  </div>

  <div class='badge-wrapper'>
    <wc-icon name="notifications"/>
    <wc-badge class='badge-anchor' value='1'/>
  </div>

  <div class='badge-wrapper'>
    <wc-icon name="notifications"/>
    <wc-badge class='badge-anchor' value='1200'/>
  </div>

  <div class='badge-wrapper'>
    <wc-icon name="notifications"/>
    <wc-badge class='badge-anchor' value='12' max='9' intent='success'/>
  </div>

  <style is:inline>
    .badge-wrapper {
      position: relative;
      display: inline-flex;
      width: 1.5rem;
      height: 1.5rem;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
    }

    .badge-anchor-simple {
      position: absolute;
      top: 0;
      right: 0;
    }

    .badge-anchor {
      position: absolute;
      top: -2px;
      left: calc(100% - 12px);
    }
  </style>

</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Accessibility</h3>

<p>
  A dot alone means nothing to a screen reader, so it is hidden from assistive technology unless it has
  a <code>label</code>. Give a count a <code>label</code> such as "3 unread messages" when the number
  alone is not enough. When the badge sits on an icon button, put the whole meaning in the button's
  <code>aria-label</code> (for example "Inbox, 3 unread") and leave the badge without a label.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={"html"} inline>
  <wc-badge value='3' label='3 unread messages'></wc-badge>
</DemoComponentCard>
